					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-405580#post-1293027</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-405580/clavis#post-1293027</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 28 Oct 2011 20:45:45 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Tirantal</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1222738</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I quite enjoy this one, the tone is fantastic in conjunction with Clef's proposal. That said, there were a few word choices that I was wondering about, as well as a couple of typos.<br /> 6-You Sardinians&#8230; is inconsistent with the rest of the piece.<br /> 6-&#8230;Tired of his suffering&#8230; It feels off that it would be God who would be suffering here, rather then referencing it being all Heaven's suffering.<br /> Just a stylistic choice, but maybe tired of this suffering would flow better?<br /> 6-&#8230;thin unholy trinity&#8230; Assuming thine was intended? Unless MC&amp;D are all slender as well :)<br /> 7-&#8230;souls on many&#8230; Was of many intended? It could be an archaic use and Im just unfamiliar with it.<br /> Cleaned up and clarified and I would gladly upvote. I especially love the corruption of the message at the last.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
